<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-20 (disposition-tranche-2-requirements.md, D6.1) - BUYER ACTIVITY TIMELINE,
        SCHEMA HALF. ROLE-NAMED CONTACT LOOKUP, explicitly permitted by ARCHITECTURE.md §1.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 DELIBERATELY UNFILTERED. DO NOT ADD Is_Buyer__c. THIS WAS AN OPEN DESIGN ITEM (O-5),
        NOW CLOSED BY THE USER'S ACCEPTED RECOMMENDATION - DO NOT RE-OPEN IT. Full reasoning is
        in the twin field's comment, objects/NDA__c/fields/Buyer__c.field-meta.xml: a buyer is
        deal-scoped, not a durable role like broker, so an active Is_Broker__c-style filter would
        gate a brand-new Contact on a checkbox with no seed population behind it.

        =====================================================================================
        RELATIONSHIP NAME: Buyer_Disposition_Offers. COLLISION CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED.
        =====================================================================================
        Every referenceTo Contact field in this repo as of this change uses one of
        Broker_Assignments, Brokered_Dispositions, Lease_Inquiries, Brokered_Opportunities,
        Brokered_BOV_Submissions, Incoming_Broker_Changes or Outgoing_Broker_Changes.
        Buyer_Disposition_Offers is free.

        =====================================================================================
        LABEL: "Buyer Contact", NOT "Buyer". "Buyer" IS ALREADY TAKEN.
        =====================================================================================
        Disposition_Offer__c.Buyer_Name__c already carries <label>Buyer</label> (free Text, the
        pre-existing analyst-typed buyer name). Labelling this lookup "Buyer" too would put two
        identically-labelled entries in the report field picker, Setup field list, Dynamic Forms
        palette and every list view column chooser, with nothing to tell them apart - the exact
        hazard this repo's other Contact-lookup fields (e.g. BOV_Submission__c.Broker__c, "Broker
        Contact") were written to avoid. "Buyer Contact" is unique on this object and mirrors the
        label chosen for the twin field on NDA__c in the same change.

        🔴 Buyer_Name__c IS NOT RETIRED OR REPOINTED BY THIS FIELD. It stays free Text and stays
        analyst-typed; nothing in this change stamps it from this lookup. Converting it, or
        wiring a stamp between the two, is out of scope here (declarative-field-and-permset-only
        deliverable) and is a decision for whoever next touches this object's Apex.

        deleteConstraint SetNull, matching every sibling Contact lookup in this repo.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 FLS: THIS FIELD IS INVISIBLE TO EVERYONE, ADMINS INCLUDED, UNTIL A PERMSET LANDS.
        =====================================================================================
        A Metadata API deployed custom field arrives with NO field permissions for any profile,
        System Administrator included. Read and edit are granted in DPEG_Disposition_Edit and
        read only in DPEG_Disposition_View in the same change - the two permission sets that
        already carry every other Disposition_Offer__c business field. DPEG_Admin_Access is not
        touched, matching how every other field on this object was granted. This file and those
        two permission sets must deploy together.
    -->
    <fullName>Buyer__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>Buyer contact for this offer. Deliberately UNFILTERED - see in-file comment; no Is_Buyer__c gate exists. Buyer_Name__c (free Text) stays as-is and is not stamped from this lookup by this change.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Pick the buyer Contact who made this offer. Not filtered by role - a buyer is often a brand-new Contact created for this deal.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Buyer Contact</label>
    <referenceTo>Contact</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Buyer Disposition Offers</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>Buyer_Disposition_Offers</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
